  "slug": "associated-oyster-3ec6",
  "summary": "Recent database and tool releases encode cell-type and spatial context into methylation, copy-number, eQTL, and single-nucleus disease resources.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the encoding of cell-type, tissue, and spatial context into reusable, queryable resources and interpretable models. CellMethMarker curates 347,514 de novo and 2.2M literature-derived cell- and tissue-type methylation markers for deconvolution, while scMRdb harmonizes 5206 GWAS summary statistics with 585 sc-eQTL datasets for cell-type-resolved Mendelian randomization. XYcellAtlas integrates single-cell, epigenomic and spatial transcriptomic data from 6764 samples across 18 cancers, and mV2G integrates 24 functional genomic evidence types across 50 human tissues. On the modeling side, ADVISE disentangles Braak-stage signals in AD snRNA-seq, and ADInteractome extracts gene interactions from neural network internal states. The ALS proteomics batch correction is a related but distinct data-quality step rather than a single-cell method. What is new is mainly the packaging of these contexts at scale with interpretable access.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
